+# Epic Breakdown: Pulseboard
+
+**Project**: Pulseboard  
+**Date**: 2026-08-10  
+**Total Epics**: 3 (E000 plus 2 product epics)  
+**Estimated Total Stories**: 10-15
+
+## Epic Dependency Map
+
+```
+E000 --> E001 --> E002
+```
+
+## Epic Prioritization
+
+### MVP Epics (Must Have)
+
+- E000: Developer Infrastructure
+- E001: Controlled Workspace Action Review
+- E002: One Reminder Delivery and Status
+
+### Enhancement Epics (Should Have)
+
+—
+
+### Future Epics (Nice to Have)
+
+— Non-goals are not future commitments.
+
+## Epic Definitions
+
+### E000: Developer Infrastructure
+
+**Value Statement**: Gives the two-engineer pilot a reliable baseline for shipping and observing the controlled action workflow.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Configure local and CI checks for the Python API and browser UI, environment boundaries for the unselected provider, deployment staging, and error observation.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] API and browser UI checks run locally.
+- [ ] CI runs lint, tests, and build.
+- [ ] Provider configuration separates non-production and live credentials.
+- [ ] Runtime and delivery failures are observable.
+
+**User Stories Summary**: test/build baseline; CI quality gates; environment configuration; runtime observation.
+
+**Dependencies**: **Depends On**: None. **Enables**: E001, E002.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+- Migrations: —
+- Models/Services: application configuration and observability boundary
+- Files/Components: repository tooling, CI workflow, API/UI test configuration, environment templates
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 3-4  
+**Priority**: P0 — Foundation  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 0
+
+### E001: Controlled Workspace Action Review
+
+**Value Statement**: Enables facilitators to turn transcripts into reviewed, workspace-private action items, retaining control over every downstream reminder.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Create workspace-scoped transcript upload, proposed-action extraction, review, editing, and explicit confirmation of text, owner, and due date. Fulfills PRM-001, PRM-002, and PRM-004.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] Uploaded transcripts produce workspace-scoped proposals.
+- [ ] A facilitator edits and explicitly confirms text, owner, and due date.
+- [ ] Scheduling is blocked before confirmation.
+- [ ] A real cross-workspace request-role probe cannot read another workspace's data.
+
+**User Stories Summary**: workspace authorization; upload and extraction; review/confirmation; eligibility guard and facilitator LARP.
+
+**Dependencies**: **Depends On**: E000. **Enables**: E002.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+- Migrations: workspace, transcript, proposed-action, and confirmed-action persistence
+- Models/Services: workspace authorization, transcript extraction, action review and confirmation service
+- Files/Components: Python API routes, browser upload/review/confirmation screens, request-role isolation tests
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 5-7  
+**Priority**: P0 — MVP critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 1
+
+### E002: One Reminder Delivery and Status
+
+**Value Statement**: Enables facilitators to follow a confirmed action through one configured reminder attempt and see its outcome.
+
+**Scope Summary**: Add a configurable reminder-provider adapter, one-reminder scheduling guard, and visible delivery status. Fulfills PRM-003 without calendar replacement or autonomous outbound messaging.
+
+**Success Criteria**:
+
+- [ ] Only confirmed actions are eligible for delivery.
+- [ ] An eligible action produces at most one provider attempt.
+- [ ] Provider selection is configuration, not product logic.
+- [ ] Status is visibly pending, sent, or failed.
+
+**User Stories Summary**: provider adapter; scheduling guard; result capture; status UI and end-to-end evidence.
+
+**Dependencies**: **Depends On**: E000, E001. **Enables**: pilot end-to-end evidence.
+
+**Touch-points (creates/modifies)**:
+- Migrations: reminder attempt and delivery-status persistence
+- Models/Services: provider adapter, scheduling guard, delivery-status service
+- Files/Components: Python API delivery endpoints/workers, browser action-status view, provider integration tests
+
+**Estimated Stories**: 2-4  
+**Priority**: P0 — MVP critical  
+**Target Phase**: Phase 2
+
+## Epic Execution Strategy
+
+| Phase | Epic | Goal | Success gate |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 0 | E000 | Reliable development and evidence baseline | Checks, CI, configuration, and observation exist |
+| 1 | E001 | Controlled, workspace-private review | Facilitator LARP completes; real negative isolation probe passes |
+| 2 | E002 | Observable follow-through | Upload-to-confirmation-to-delivery path shows honest status |
+
+## Risk Mitigation by Epic
+
+| Epic | Primary Risk | Mitigation Strategy |
+|---|---|---|
+| E000 | Product work cannot be evaluated or operated | Establish checks and observation first |
+| E001 | Human control or tenant isolation is bypassed | Separate proposal/confirmation and run a real negative probe |
+| E002 | Provider uncertainty or duplicate sends erodes trust | Configurable adapter, one-attempt guard, visible status |
+
+## Success Metrics by Epic
+
+| Epic | Key Metric | Target | Measurement |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| E000 | Planned checks runnable | API/UI checks and CI available | Local and CI evidence |
+| E001 | Proposal review rate | >=80% | Workspace-scoped events |
+| E002 | Unowned overdue actions | 30% reduction | Pilot baseline and weekly review |
+
+## Epic Concurrency Waves & Rebase Cadence
+
+| Wave | Epics | May run in parallel? | Starts when | Daily rebase cadence |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| 0 | E000 | No | Project start | N/A — merge before Wave 1 |
+| 1 | E001 | No | E000 merged to `main` | Rebase before new story work if `main` advances |
+| 2 | E002 | No | E001 merged to `main` | Rebase before new story work if `main` advances |
+
+The plan is serial because E002 consumes E001's confirmed-action model and guard. This three-epic plan remains below the Build four-epic complexity gate. Run the recommended decorrelated `/project-analyze` before any `/epic-specify`.
